+The wrapper prints `Original-layout check workspace (retained): ...`. It keeps that workspace for inspection, runs the supplied command from the reconstructed **repository root**, and propagates the child command's exit status. Handled wrapper setup failures exit with status 2; an uncaught malformed-map shape error can instead exit with status 1. A child can also return status 2, so inspect the diagnostic output rather than classifying a failure by exit status alone. A printed workspace path alone does not mean the requested check passed. Historical checkers may write logs and build products there; inspect their source and resource requirements before running them.
 
 The generic interface is `python3 proofs/replay_original_layout.py -- COMMAND ARGUMENTS...`. It does not change into `proofs/` or `proofs/research/` for the child. Commands in an older guide must retain their documented working-directory assumptions inside the reconstructed workspace. [verify_project.py](verify_project.py) and [verify_release.py](verify_release.py) are forwarding wrappers for their original-layout counterparts, not independent whole-repository verifiers.
 
